# Copy this file to agent-manager.env (git-ignored) and fill in your own values.
# launch.bat reads this file and sets each KEY=VALUE as an environment variable before
# starting the pipeline -- see README.md's "Configuration" section for the full reference.

# Required -- absolute path to the repo this pipeline operates on.
AGENT_MANAGER_REPO_ROOT=C:\path\to\your\repo

# Where queue/, instances/, and your own local task-source/applier scripts live.
# Defaults to AGENT_MANAGER_REPO_ROOT if unset -- uncomment to put pipeline state
# somewhere else (e.g. a subfolder, matching a consumer project's own backend/agent-pipeline/).
#AGENT_MANAGER_PIPELINE_DIR=C:\path\to\your\repo\agent-pipeline

# Path (or comma-separated list of paths) to a script the CLI entry points require() once,
# for its side effect of calling registerTaskSource/updateTaskSource for out-of-tree task
# sources. Omit for only this package's built-in sources. Example: the programming-hygiene
# plugin, which owns observability/performance/function-length/architecture/unused-export:
#AGENT_MANAGER_REGISTER_PATH=/path/to/agent-manager-hygiene/register.js
# (The dashboard's Plugins tab writes plugins.json beside this file, which supersedes the
# var above once present.)
#
# The dashboard's Chat panel is system-wide: it is always rooted at THIS repo and can
# read/edit every enabled plugin repo (dirname of each plugins.json registerPath) plus
# every projects.json repoRoot -- regardless of which project the pipeline is pointed at.
# No env var configures this; the root list is derived from plugins.json + projects.json.
#
# Chat "make GPU space": on every local-provider chat message the dashboard kills
# worker-1's in-flight draft (always) and worker-reasoning's / the reviewer's model call
# (only if it started less than _REASONING_MAX_AGE_S ago), then runs the turn so it gets
# the resident model immediately. Killed worker tasks are requeued to pending/ with no
# retry-budget cost. Set _CHAT_PREEMPT=false to disable entirely.
#AGENT_MANAGER_CHAT_PREEMPT=true
#AGENT_MANAGER_CHAT_PREEMPT_REASONING_MAX_AGE_S=180

# A personal-notes vault, if you use the 'secondbrain' built-in source. Omit otherwise.
#SECOND_BRAIN_DIR=C:\path\to\your\vault

# The domain name stamped on trouble_log/arch_review/arch_discovery/unused_export tasks --
# must match a real key in your AGENT_MANAGER_DOMAINS_PATH file. Defaults to 'default'.
#AGENT_MANAGER_DEFAULT_DOMAIN=default

# e.g. https://github.com/you/repo/compare/main... -- appended with the pushed branch
# name in log output. Omit if you don't want a compare-URL link generated.
#AGENT_MANAGER_COMPARE_URL_BASE=https://github.com/you/repo/compare/main...

# Ollama connection -- defaults shown, uncomment to override.
#OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434

# TokenFold -- transparent token-compression proxy between this pipeline and Ollama,
# on by default: launch.sh starts it from a standalone checkout next to this repo if one
# exists, else from the vendored snapshot at vendor/tokenfold (self-contained, no second
# download; venv auto-provisioned on first launch), reroutes OLLAMA_URL through it, and
# shows savings in the dashboard's TokenFold tab (full detail at
# http://localhost:9339/tokenfold/dashboard). Set AGENT_MANAGER_TOKENFOLD=false to opt out.
#AGENT_MANAGER_TOKENFOLD=false
#TOKENFOLD_DIR=/path/to/tokenfold
#TOKENFOLD_PORT=9339
# PromptForge: a separate local ComfyUI-driven image-shot generator, embedded as the
# "PromptForge" dashboard tab (its own repo/server; not an agent-manager plugin).
#PROMPTFORGE_URL=http://localhost:7430
# AdForge: a separate local advertisement-pipeline orchestrator, embedded as the
# "AdForge" dashboard tab (its own repo/server; not an agent-manager plugin). It
# sequences ScriptForge/PromptForge/VoiceForge/CutForge/PostForge (ports 7430-7435)
# into a finished ad. See SecondBrain/Projects/adforge-project-status-and-backlog.md.
#ADFORGE_URL=http://localhost:7431
#LOCAL_MODEL=qwen3.8:27b-q4_K_M

# Adhoc drafting runs entirely on the local model (2026-09-01) in a tiered ladder:
# harness-search -> read-only agentic -> write agentic (real edit/write/run_bash in an
# isolated git worktree). The write tier is the primary path.
#AGENT_MANAGER_LOCAL_AGENTIC_WRITE=true              # false -> disable the write tier; a
#                                                     task the cheaper tiers can't do then
#                                                     blocks for a human instead
#AGENT_MANAGER_LOCAL_AGENTIC_WRITE_MAX_TURNS=20
#AGENT_MANAGER_LOCAL_AGENTIC_ADHOC=true              # optional read-only agentic tier 2,
#                                                     tried ahead of the write tier
# Turn budget for the (opt-in only) Claude adhoc draft path -- see AGENT_MANAGER_CLAUDE_SOURCES.
#AGENT_MANAGER_ADHOC_MAX_TURNS=60

# BROWNFIELD product_spec outline doc. A mode:"brownfield" (or auto-detected) product_spec
# request is decomposed into ordered AC-NNN section candidates here by product_spec_outline,
# then drafted one section at a time by product_spec_section -- all on the local model, no
# subscription agent. Defaults to <repoRoot>/Docs/PRODUCT_SPEC_OUTLINE.md.
#AGENT_MANAGER_PRODUCT_SPEC_OUTLINE_CANDIDATES_PATH=

# Dashboard port -- defaults to 7420.
#AGENT_MANAGER_DASHBOARD_PORT=7420

# GPU headroom guard (src/gpu-guard.js) -- checked once per worker/reviewer tick, before
# any real Ollama call. If free VRAM is below the minimum it tries, in order:
#   1. POST <comfy>/free  -- asks a standalone ComfyUI to unload its models (it keeps
#      running and reloads on the next prompt); this is the usual contention case.
#   2. If still starved, and TheAgent (a separate local app-management server) reports
#      an allowlisted app running, asks TheAgent to stop it via its tracked start/stop
#      API -- not a raw kill.
# No-ops entirely if nvidia-smi / ComfyUI / TheAgent aren't present.
# Raise MIN_FREE_VRAM_MB to a bit above your local model's load size (e.g. ~18000 for a
# 27B q4 that needs ~17GB) so the guard actually fires before Ollama calls start timing out.
#AGENT_MANAGER_MIN_FREE_VRAM_MB=4096
#AGENT_MANAGER_THEAGENT_URL=http://localhost:4519
#AGENT_MANAGER_COMFY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8188
#AGENT_MANAGER_GPU_YIELD_APPS=comfyui,n8n

# ComfyUI GPU lease -- the other direction of the same coordination. When PromptForge
# starts ComfyUI for a generation that wouldn't fit alongside the resident local model,
# it writes this lease file; while it's held (fresh) local-worker.sh / review-runner.sh
# yield their tick and gpu-guard.js leaves ComfyUI + Ollama alone. Absent/expired/stomped
# -> the pipeline behaves exactly as without this feature. An explicit `scripts/launch.sh`
# (or the dashboard's Start Pipeline) deletes the lease -- a hand start wins the GPU.
# The path MUST match PromptForge's COMFY_LEASE_PATH.
#AGENT_MANAGER_COMFY_LEASE_PATH=~/.local/state/agent-manager/comfyui-lease.json
#AGENT_MANAGER_COMFY_LEASE_TTL_S=90    # lease is stale if refreshedAt is older than this
#AGENT_MANAGER_COMFY_LEASE_MAX_S=900   # hard ceiling: ignored past this age regardless of refresh

# Claude Code CLI backend (src/claude-client.js) -- FULLY OPTIONAL (2026-09-01). Nothing
# in the pipeline requires it: adhoc drafts on the local model (tiered agentic ladder,
# above), review is always local, and research_task -- the one path with no local
# equivalent, since WebSearch/WebFetch are Claude-only -- blocks cleanly with a legible
# reason when Claude isn't configured (rather than wedging). Set CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
# + list sources in AGENT_MANAGER_CLAUDE_SOURCES to route those sources' plan+implement
# passes through a Claude Pro/Max/Team/Enterprise SUBSCRIPTION (not the metered API).
# Setup: `claude setup-token` once (needs a browser login to the subscription account),
# then export the printed value as CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN in the environment this
# pipeline's daemons run under -- NOT here, since this file is read into every daemon's
# env and CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN is a credential, same reasoning as never committing an
# API key to this example file. Do not set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN
# anywhere in this pipeline's environment -- either one silently outranks the
# subscription token and switches billing to the metered API (claude-client.js also
# strips both from its own child process as a second layer of defense, but the daemons'
# own env should never carry them in the first place).
#AGENT_MANAGER_CLAUDE_SOURCES=research_task     # e.g. to enable web research; unset -> pure-local
#CLAUDE_MODEL=sonnet
#CLAUDE_TIMEOUT_MS=300000

# --- Dashboard LAN access (Android companion app) ---
# Default binding is loopback-only. Set HOST to 0.0.0.0 to let other devices (the
# companion app) reach the dashboard; mutating requests from non-loopback callers then
# require the TOKEN as "Authorization: Bearer <token>" (reads are never gated).
#AGENT_MANAGER_DASHBOARD_HOST=0.0.0.0
#AGENT_MANAGER_DASHBOARD_TOKEN=pick-a-long-random-string

# --- Task history repo (task-repo-sync.js) ---
# A DEDICATED git repo (not this pipeline's own code repo -- see task-repo-sync.js's own
# header) that every task's record gets committed into, at tasks/<id>.json, updated in
# place across the task's whole lifecycle. Optional: unset means this integration simply
# doesn't run (fails open), same as every other optional integration in this file. Create
# an empty repo with a real initial commit on its default branch first (`git init -b main
# && git commit --allow-empty -m init && git push -u origin main`) -- this pipeline never
# creates the repo itself, only commits into an already-existing one.
#AGENT_MANAGER_TASK_REPO_URL=https://github.com/your-org/your-project-tasks
